WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.001 --> 00:00:07.246
"Does Resveratrol Benefit Our Metabolic Health?"

00:00:07.391 --> 00:00:09.420
To see if the amount
of resveratrol you get

00:00:09.420 --> 00:00:11.460
from drinking red wine
might be beneficial,

00:00:11.460 --> 00:00:14.640
researchers looked to
the Chianti region of Tuscany

00:00:14.640 --> 00:00:16.680
to determine whether the levels
achieved through diet

00:00:16.680 --> 00:00:18.900
help protect
against long-term frailty,

00:00:18.900 --> 00:00:21.840
inflammation,
cardiovascular disease,

00:00:21.840 --> 00:00:22.860
cancer, or death.

00:00:22.860 --> 00:00:24.180
And the answer?

00:00:24.180 --> 00:00:26.280
None of the above.

00:00:26.280 --> 00:00:29.100
The amount of resveratrol
flowing through their systems

00:00:29.100 --> 00:00:31.500
didn't correlate with any
of the health outcomes studied

00:00:31.500 --> 00:00:32.700
over nine years of follow-up.

00:00:32.700 --> 00:00:34.320
This is surprising

00:00:34.320 --> 00:00:36.660
even if only because of
the confounding factors

00:00:36.660 --> 00:00:38.220
associated
with wine consumption.

00:00:38.220 --> 00:00:41.340
Wine drinkers may be
less likely to smoke

00:00:41.340 --> 00:00:42.540
and tend to have higher IQ,

00:00:42.540 --> 00:00:44.280
higher parental
education levels,

00:00:44.280 --> 00:00:46.140
and higher
socioeconomic status,

00:00:46.140 --> 00:00:47.940
which would be expected
to correlate

00:00:47.940 --> 00:00:49.320
with better health outcomes.

00:00:49.320 --> 00:00:52.020
In contrast, beer drinkers
suffer the opposite—

00:00:52.020 --> 00:00:54.420
lower IQ, parental education,
and social class.

00:00:54.420 --> 00:00:57.420
The average IQ
of wine-drinking men is 113,

00:00:57.420 --> 00:01:01.320
compared to 95
among beer-drinking men.

00:01:01.320 --> 00:01:03.720
Yet still, there appeared
to be no correlation

00:01:03.720 --> 00:01:06.000
between resveratrol exposure
and well-being.

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:08.700
This may be because
wine-drinking populations

00:01:08.700 --> 00:01:11.400
may only be averaging
less than a milligram

00:01:11.400 --> 00:01:13.200
of resveratrol a day.

00:01:14.160 --> 00:01:16.980
Some "experts" recommend
a daily dose

00:01:16.980 --> 00:01:18.960
of 1 gram of resveratrol,

00:01:18.960 --> 00:01:21.240
based on the dosing used
in laboratory animal studies.

00:01:21.240 --> 00:01:23.400
How much red wine
would you have to drink

00:01:23.400 --> 00:01:24.180
to get that much?

00:01:24.180 --> 00:01:27.540
Eight thousand glasses a day.

00:01:27.540 --> 00:01:28.800
Not a fan of red wine?

00:01:28.800 --> 00:01:30.540
A couple thousand gallons

00:01:30.540 --> 00:01:32.040
of white wine a day
would do it,

00:01:32.040 --> 00:01:34.680
or 5,000 pounds of apples
or grapes,

00:01:34.680 --> 00:01:37.020
50,000 pounds of peanuts,

00:01:37.020 --> 00:01:39.360
a couple thousand pounds
of chocolate,

00:01:39.360 --> 00:01:43.740
or nearly a million bottles
of beer on the wall.

00:01:43.740 --> 00:01:45.600
The natural levels
of resveratrol

00:01:45.600 --> 00:01:47.760
found in foods and beverages
is not considered

00:01:47.760 --> 00:01:49.980
to be sufficient
to elicit health effects,

00:01:49.980 --> 00:01:51.240
but that doesn't
necessarily mean

00:01:51.240 --> 00:01:52.560
supplements wouldn't work.

00:01:53.100 --> 00:01:56.700
However, the bioavailability
of even high-dose resveratrol

00:01:56.700 --> 00:01:57.960
has been called into question.

00:01:57.960 --> 00:02:01.140
Maximum blood levels after
resveratrol supplementation

00:02:01.140 --> 00:02:03.180
can be as low as 40 nanomolar,

00:02:03.180 --> 00:02:05.280
which is more than
a hundred times lower

00:02:05.280 --> 00:02:09.780
than the 5,000 to 250,000
nanomoles used in vitro

00:02:09.780 --> 00:02:11.460
to demonstrate
resveratrol effects.

00:02:11.460 --> 00:02:14.040
Even a five-gram dose
of resveratrol

00:02:14.040 --> 00:02:16.560
may fall short
of the required level.

00:02:16.560 --> 00:02:18.960
This is in contrast to rodents,

00:02:18.960 --> 00:02:21.900
in which blood levels
of 32,000 have been reported.

00:02:22.560 --> 00:02:25.320
Resveratrol is rapidly absorbed
in humans

00:02:25.320 --> 00:02:28.380
but is rapidly metabolized
in our intestine and liver;

00:02:28.380 --> 00:02:31.320
so, very little
free resveratrol remains.

00:02:31.320 --> 00:02:35.160
But there are about 20
resveratrol-derived metabolites

00:02:35.160 --> 00:02:37.260
that can end up in circulation
at much higher levels,

00:02:37.260 --> 00:02:39.060
like 20,000 nanomolar,

00:02:39.060 --> 00:02:42.000
that might have biological
activity of their own.

00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:44.580
What about using
the turmeric trick

00:02:44.580 --> 00:02:46.080
of adding black pepper
to suppress

00:02:46.080 --> 00:02:48.600
our body's natural
detoxification mechanisms?

00:02:48.600 --> 00:02:50.520
It works in mice.

00:02:50.520 --> 00:02:53.700
The black pepper compound
piperine

00:02:53.700 --> 00:02:56.040
increases maximum
blood concentrations

00:02:56.040 --> 00:02:58.620
of resveratrol
more than 1,000 percent,

00:02:58.620 --> 00:03:00.600
but, unfortunately, it failed

00:03:00.600 --> 00:03:03.360
to significantly alter
blood levels in people.

00:03:04.020 --> 00:03:06.600
In a 2014 medical journal
editorial entitled

00:03:06.600 --> 00:03:08.640
"The resveratrol fiasco,"

00:03:08.640 --> 00:03:12.240
the Editor-in-Chief summarized
the state of the science:

00:03:12.240 --> 00:03:14.820
"The conclusions
are quite clear-cut:

00:03:14.820 --> 00:03:17.220
after more than 20 years
of well-funded research,

00:03:17.220 --> 00:03:21.240
resveratrol has no proven
human activity."

00:03:22.140 --> 00:03:23.580
However,
since that publication,

00:03:23.580 --> 00:03:26.160
more than 150
human clinical trials

00:03:26.160 --> 00:03:26.820
have been published.

00:03:26.820 --> 00:03:28.260
What's the update?

00:03:28.920 --> 00:03:32.700
Resveratrol was initially
envisaged as an antioxidant,

00:03:32.700 --> 00:03:35.100
but meta-analyses
of randomized controlled trials

00:03:35.100 --> 00:03:37.800
of resveratrol supplements
failed to find

00:03:37.800 --> 00:03:40.380
clinically or even statistically
significant effects

00:03:40.380 --> 00:03:42.180
on systemic markers
of oxidative stress,

00:03:42.180 --> 00:03:45.060
helping to explain the lack
of apparent DNA protection.

00:03:45.780 --> 00:03:49.560
Maybe it only helps with
the metabolically compromised?

00:03:49.560 --> 00:03:51.840
As one resveratrol review asked,

00:03:51.840 --> 00:03:53.460
"What conclusions would we draw

00:03:53.460 --> 00:03:55.440
about the efficacy
of penicillin

00:03:55.440 --> 00:03:57.180
if it had been tested
only among persons

00:03:57.180 --> 00:03:58.320
in the pink of condition?"

00:03:59.460 --> 00:04:01.440
Resveratrol does not appear
to improve

00:04:01.440 --> 00:04:03.589
the metabolic function
of nonobese,

00:04:03.589 --> 00:04:04.680
nondiabetic individuals,

00:04:04.680 --> 00:04:07.080
or even benefit
overweight nondiabetics,

00:04:07.080 --> 00:04:08.580
nor does it help people
lose weight,

00:04:08.580 --> 00:04:10.680
but resveratrol may help

00:04:10.680 --> 00:04:12.960
with blood sugar control
in diabetics.

00:04:13.860 --> 00:04:15.900
For almost all outcomes

00:04:15.900 --> 00:04:17.700
measured in randomized
controlled trials

00:04:17.700 --> 00:04:19.500
of type 2 diabetes,
metabolic syndrome,

00:04:19.500 --> 00:04:21.120
or nonalcoholic
fatty liver disease,

00:04:21.120 --> 00:04:23.700
the effects of resveratrol
were trivial,

00:04:23.700 --> 00:04:25.920
but a meta-analysis did find

00:04:25.920 --> 00:04:29.220
that in doses ranging
from 5 to 500 milligrams

00:04:29.220 --> 00:04:32.040
twice a day resulted
in an average 20-point drop

00:04:32.040 --> 00:04:33.300
in fasting blood sugars.

00:04:33.300 --> 00:04:35.220
There was also
a significant benefit

00:04:35.220 --> 00:04:37.260
for longer-term
blood sugar control,

00:04:37.260 --> 00:04:39.600
though this only appeared
to be the case

00:04:39.600 --> 00:04:41.040
in shorter-term studies.

00:04:41.040 --> 00:04:43.500
What is the point
of better longer-term control,

00:04:43.500 --> 00:04:44.820
if it only works in studies

00:04:44.820 --> 00:04:46.500
lasting less than three months.

00:04:47.160 --> 00:04:50.340
Diabetic foot ulcers
are the leading cause

00:04:50.340 --> 00:04:52.680
of lower-limb amputations
in diabetics.

00:04:52.680 --> 00:04:55.140
A randomized, double-blind,
placebo-controlled trial

00:04:55.140 --> 00:04:57.480
of 50 milligrams of resveratrol
twice a day

00:04:57.480 --> 00:05:00.840
showed accelerated healing
of diabetic foot ulcers

00:05:00.840 --> 00:05:03.960
by about 1 centimeter
over placebo within 60 days.

00:05:03.960 --> 00:05:06.360
So, at least there's
one condition it may help.

00:05:06.360 --> 00:05:10.680
Next, I'll cover resveratrol
for joint, brain,

00:05:10.680 --> 00:05:11.760
and bone health,

00:05:11.760 --> 00:05:14.400
and then I'll talk
about the downsides.

